Simple project divided to 3 files:

main.py - manages the program flow, initialize and run the program until finish.
game.py - all the program's logic functions.
board.py - containing the board and the function that prints the board.

inside main.py, main() will run in a while loop till the game finish.
going to call all the functions and maintain the counter (to know if it's a draw...),
and the variables that tell whose turn is it.

game.py containing a list of tuples with indexes, to know if there is a winner,
and also the following functions:
user_choice() - ask the user to type a number (1-9), and validate that it's valid (int, (1-9), not occupied).
occupied_cell() - validate that the cell is not occupied.
mark_cell() - markes the cell the user choose as occupied by the user.
next_turn() - move the turn to the next player.
winning() - checkes if we have a winner, if so, prints the board and a winning message.
draw() - called when we don't have any remainig cells, prints the board and print a draw message.

board.py containig the board and the function print_board() that prints the board in a nice way.